Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

## 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use the **constructor** / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` for per-test setup/teardown.

---

## 2. Once before first / after last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // static — runs once before first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Can_Place_Order() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

## 3. Once per assembly (before any / after all tests)

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // tear down
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Once for the entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

## Quick-reference table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? | Context type |
|-------|-----------|----------------|--------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No | `TestContext` |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **Yes** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **Yes** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **Yes** | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, on any class) for a *global* cross-cutting hook that fires for every test in the run — handy for logging or diagnostics without touching each test class.
